  "module": {
    "id": "roster-repair-feasibility",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "template": {
      "id": "complete-a-commitment",
      "version": 1
    },
    "title": "Repair a published restaurant roster",
    "question": "Which supplied complete repairs cover every remaining service within the recorded staffing and payroll limits?",
    "description": "Compare supplied complete repairs for a published roster. Every remaining authored position is checked; a preferred repair is established only among these alternatives.",
    "units": {
      "time": "minute",
      "timeOrigin": "Monday 00:00 of one fictional week; one local clock without a daylight-saving transition",
      "money": "USD cent",
      "count": "position"
    },
    "assumptions": [
      "This bounded comparison evaluates supplied complete repairs; it does not search every possible employee assignment or generate service demand.",
      "Every position has an authored role and fixed positive interval. Required breaks must be omitted from working availability and explicitly covered by a supplied repair.",
      "Fees are flat accepted amounts per complete assignment. Different durations are counted accurately for hours; no hourly pay, proration, overtime premium or tax is inferred.",
      "The retained baseline sums published assignments after removing explicitly unpaid cancellations. Changed positions compare assigned people with the published roster, not employee disruption, consent or fairness.",
      "Earlier work is retained as totals and latest shift ends. Declared weekly-hours and rest limits are assumptions, not a labor-law assessment. Existing bookings are checked for capacity, not retrospectively audited for rest.",
      "A calculated proposal does not obtain staff agreement, notify employees or publish a roster. Demand forecasts and actual operation require separate records or integrations."
    ],
